-- title:
--   The subdivided large sieve for odd bilinear sums
-- statement:
--   For finite sets of odd natural numbers in real intervals of lengths at least two, suppose the frequencies $4j\alpha$ stay at circular distance at least $\delta>0$ from zero for $1\le j\le M$, where $M\ge1$. The associated bilinear exponential sum is bounded by the product of the two coefficient $\ell^2$ norms and
--   $$\sqrt{(n_1-n_0)/2+\delta^{-1}}\,\sqrt{(m_1-m_0)/(2M)+1}.$$
--   The interval endpoints and spacing hypotheses are retained explicitly.
-- source:
--   Terence Tao, Every odd number greater than 1 is the sum of at most five primes, https://arxiv.org/abs/1201.6656, Sections 3 and 5. Original Lean source: Theorems/Thm_TaoFivePrimes_odd_interval_bilinear_large_sieve_proved.lean, lines 32-54.

